"[2511.12027] GCAgent: Long-Video Understanding via Schematic and Narrative Episodic Memory (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.12027)\nciteturn6183view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.12027\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 161\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 15 Nov 2025]\nL9: # Title:GCAgent: Long-Video Understanding via Schematic and Narrative Episodic Memory\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Jeong Hun Yeo , cite6†Sangyun Chung , cite7†Sungjune Park , cite8†Dae Hoe Kim , cite9†Jinyoung Moon , cite10†Yong Man Ro L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled GCAgent: Long-Video Understanding via Schematic and Narrative Episodic Memory, by Jeong Hun Yeo and 5 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite11†View PDF cite12†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Long-video understanding remains a significant challenge for Multimodal Large Language Models (MLLMs) due to inherent token limitations and the complexity of capturing long-term temporal dependencies. Existing methods often fail to capture the global context and complex event relationships necessary for deep video reasoning. To address this, we introduce GCAgent, a novel Global-Context-Aware Agent framework that achieves comprehensive long-video understanding.\nL17: Our core innovation is the Schematic and Narrative Episodic Memory. This memory structurally models events and their causal and temporal relations into a concise, organized context, fundamentally resolving the long-term dependency problem. Operating in a multi-stage Perception-Action-Reflection cycle, our GCAgent utilizes a Memory Manager to retrieve relevant episodic context for robust, context-aware inference.\nL18: Extensive experiments confirm that GCAgent significantly enhances long-video understanding, achieving up to 23.5\\% accuracy improvement on the Video-MME Long split over a strong MLLM baseline.\nL19: Furthermore, our framework establishes state-of-the-art performance among comparable 7B-scale MLLMs, achieving 73.4\\% accuracy on the Long split and the highest overall average (71.9\\%) on the Video-MME benchmark, validating our agent-based reasoning paradigm and structured memory for cognitively-inspired long-video understanding.\nL20: Subjects:  | Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite13†arXiv:2511.12027 [cs.CV]\nL22:    | (or cite14†arXiv:2511.12027v1 [cs.CV] for this version)\nL23:    | cite15†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.12027†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: JeongHun Yeo [cite16†view email ]\nL27: [v1] Sat, 15 Nov 2025 04:29:00 UTC (681 KB)\nL28: \nL29: Full-text links:\nL30: \nL31: ## Access Paper:\nL32: \nL33: View a PDF of the paper titled GCAgent: Long-Video Understanding via Schematic and Narrative Episodic Memory, by Jeong Hun Yeo and 5 other authors\nL34: \nL35:   * cite11†View PDF L36:   * cite12†HTML (experimental) L37:   * cite17†TeX Source L38: \nL39: cite18†view license L40: ### Current browse context:\nL41: \nL42: cs.CV\nL43: \nL44: cite19†< prev |   cite20†next > L45: \nL46: cite21†new | cite22†recent | cite23†2025-11 L47: \nL48: Change to browse by:\nL49: \nL50: cite24†cs L51: cite25†cs.AI L52: \nL53: ### References & Citations\nL54: \nL55:   * cite26†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L56:   * cite27†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L57:   * cite28†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L58: \nL59: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL60: \nL61: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL62: \nL63: [Button: ×]\nL64: \nL65: loading